A||||7||87GT||Motor Mount Replacement?||||5||
Z||000000||87GT||02-19-2000||10:29 PM||||My 87GT seems to be a bit shackey to me.  Whenever I am at idle, I notice that the car shakes a little bit.  I also notice sometimes I hear sort of a tapping type thump noise whenever I go over small bumps in the road or whenever I shift gears.  I think it bad motor mounts.  I noticed the dog bone on top is pretty much shot, but I need to know what else would need to be replaced to solve this annoying problem.  BTW, you 5-Sp V6 drivers please tell me what your trip meter says when you have a quarter tank of gas left in your car.  I am curious to know. Thanks for any help. 8-)||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||02-19-2000||10:34 PM||||1/4 tank left. Mine is usually in the vicinity of 180-190 miles. This is about 80% highway driving at 70mph. I have an '88 with the 11.9(12) gallon tank. It is a 5-speed v-6.<P>For motor mounts, in the next month or so, I plan to install an "ultimate" dog-bone, and replace both tranny mounts. The lower engine mount seems fine, and I don't think it is a very high wear item.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 02-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GT||02-19-2000||10:38 PM||||Okay, I usually have 155-165 at a quarter.  I drive 10 miles to work and 2 miles to school then about 8 miles back home.  A lot of stop and go.  My car has a 12 gallon also.  Or so it says.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mwbackus||02-19-2000||11:15 PM||||My formula runs out of gas long before it even reaches 1/4 tank.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  <BR>I guess I'll have to fix that some day... sigh.  <P>Note:<BR>I believe Checker Auto stocks a Niehoff GA-61 replacement fuel sender ($17.95). They also have the Holley #12-903 255 L/hr high flow fuel pumps for only $149.00.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||02-20-2000||01:27 AM||||My 85 GT had the same thumping sound during hard gear changes, usually first to second. It turned out to be a worn out dogbone and a separated tranny mount. I suggest replacing the dogbone immediately, it's easy to do. Most of my clunking went away when I did this. I still need to replace the lower mount sometime this spring when the weather gets nicer.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phaeton||02-20-2000||03:25 AM||||About 160 with 1/4, but the tank has never accepted more than 11.2 and that was when the Fiero quit across the street from the gas station.  No funny clunks since replacing the dogbone.||||reg||1
Z||000006||87GT||02-20-2000||10:33 AM||||Thanks guys for letting me know for sure that it is that darn dog bone. 8-)  ||||reg||12
Z||000007||Uaana||02-22-2000||01:18 AM||||Well since we are on the topic.. I get that little thud noise on take offs. And it didn't have it before I changed my dogbone (old one was shot). So I'm thinking that the new stiff part was too stiff for the older worn parts and something else gave way.. now with all that said...<BR>How hard is it to change the motor/tranny mounts? can this be done by one person with only a floor jack/jack stands.. ect ect?<BR>thanks in advance.<BR>||||reg||5
